          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "image_url": "https://review-images.judgeme.com/barreletics/1780166108__img_3722__original.jpeg?quality=80&width=1024",
            "title": "Consistent grip. Real confidence.",
            "body": "I have tried several brands of grips socks. The grip wears off, my toes slip and my Pilates form suffers. Since I have started use the barreletics grip shoes, those days are gone. I know have more confidence in my poses and the grip is consistent. Not to mention they are easy to put on and easy to wash. The mesh bag that they come in is very useful. It is big enough to hold my grip gloves for easy storing and transportation to class.",
            "author": "Leslie S.",
            "location": "Katy, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "photo2": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "image_url": "https://review-images.judgeme.com/barreletics/1774226614__img_9682__original.jpeg?quality=80&width=1024",
            "title": "Great for travel yoga.",
            "body": "Use these for heated yoga and they are great when I travel and want to practice some yoga in my hotel room.",
            "author": "Jo-z",
            "location": "Baltimore, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "photo3": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "image_url": "https://review-images.judgeme.com/barreletics/1778161226__9063__original.jpg?quality=80&width=1024",
            "title": "Best for barre & Pilates.",
            "body": "These grippy shoes are the best most comfortable footwear for my barre and palates classes. I love them",
            "author": "B P.",
            "location": "Philadelphia, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "text1": {
          "type": "text_review",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Way too expensive? Game changer.",
            "body": "I looked at these Pilates shoes for over a year thinking 'Way too expensive.' Well, I can't tell you how much I spent on Pilates socks that got ruined and stretched out of shape in no time. They never made me feel secure in my footage. Then as a birthday gift to myself, I got these. Game changer.",
            "author": "Gwen M.",
            "location": "Queens, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "text2": {
          "type": "text_review",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Skeptical. Worth it.",
            "body": "I'll admit I was skeptical spending so much on a pair of 'socks', however these were so worth it in the end. These grip the floor in class while doing lunges and side planks that you're not budging. In the usual half toe socks I'd wear, you'd get a toe wedgie and/or start sliding which does not help with stability.",
            "author": "Amy S.",
            "location": "Pittsburgh, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "text3": {
          "type": "text_review",
          "settings": {
            "title": "After the first class…",
            "body": "I was looking for a 'good' pair of Pilates socks and came across what I thought was a ridiculously priced alternative. I sat on the idea for a couple of weeks but finally decided to take the plunge. After my first class… [game changer].",
            "author": "Wendy B.",
            "location": "Grayslake, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "text4": {
          "type": "text_review",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Always in my bag.",
            "body": "I'm a Pilates instructor and I love throwing these in my bag to keep on me at all times. I can comfortably use them for any and all moves.",
            "author": "Jennifer K.",
            "location": "Pilates instructor",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "text5": {
          "type": "text_review",
          "settings": {
            "title": "No more slipping.",
            "body": "The lagree shoes are fantastic for reformer Pilates as well as mat Pilates and barre. No more concerns about slipping means better performance. Absolutely love them!",
            "author": "Fedra P.",
            "location": "Widnes, GB",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "text6": {
          "type": "text_review",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Turned my whole class on.",
            "body": "I use these Grippys exclusively for Pilates and have turned many on to them! They are perfect for no slip and precision and I'm a 7-8 class a week person and have 2 pairs that I lightly clean with the same gentle wipes we use for equipment.",
            "author": "Lauren",
            "location": "Indianapolis, US",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "featured1": {
